+dnl Veda's C library is musl's, which has functions Veda does not carry out:
+dnl they would be found, and fail when called. Veda starts a program in one
+dnl step, from its file (posix_spawn): there is no fork() to copy a process
+dnl with, nor exec() to replace a program (_posixsubprocess spawns instead),
+dnl and no dynamic loading. Its signals are synchronous: no interval timers
+dnl or alarms. Its files have no links, hard or symbolic (but for the names of
+dnl shared memory objects, in /dev/shm, which sem_open links), and there are
+dnl no named pipes or device files to make. It has no pseudo-terminals, and a
+dnl few system calls fail with ENOSYS (setting a clock, chroot, resizing a
+dnl mapping, copying in the kernel, reading another process's memory). Its
+dnl network interfaces are not listed as Linux's are (if_nameindex() asks a
+dnl netlink socket). The empty libdl.a, librt.a and libutil.a that musl
+dnl installs would find some again: they are not looked in.
+AS_VAR_IF([ac_sys_system], [Veda], [
+  for name in fork fork1 vfork forkpty execv fexecve dlopen \
+      alarm getitimer setitimer clock_settime \
+      link linkat symlink symlinkat mkfifo mkfifoat mknod mknodat \
+      openpty posix_openpt grantpt unlockpt ptsname ptsname_r \
+      chroot mremap sendfile splice copy_file_range process_vm_readv \
+      sched_rr_get_interval if_nameindex; do
+    AS_VAR_PUSHDEF([func_var], [ac_cv_func_$name])
+    AS_VAR_SET([func_var], [no])
+    AS_VAR_POPDEF([func_var])
+  done
+  for name in dl_dlopen rt_clock_settime util_openpty bsd_openpty \
+      util_forkpty bsd_forkpty; do
+    AS_VAR_PUSHDEF([lib_var], [ac_cv_lib_$name])
+    AS_VAR_SET([lib_var], [no])
+    AS_VAR_POPDEF([lib_var])
+  done
+])
+dnl Veda links every program with its C library, musl, whose release the
+dnl build names: platform.libc_ver() gives it.
